From: Chokri Hammedi <52697989+blue0x1@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] graphics: clear from color metadata with a shader where conditional rendering is off

When a game samples a color target it fast-cleared, KytyPS5 checks the
target's DCC/CMASK metadata for a clear key. With conditional rendering a
compute pass finds the key and a predicated clear applies it, so the CPU
never waits. Patch 0006 turns conditional rendering off on the PS4's GPUs
(they hang on SET_PREDICATION), and the metadata was then read back on the
CPU, which waits for the GPU to finish everything first. Invincible VS
(PPSA30568) does that 29 times a frame in its menu: 446 ms of a 558 ms
frame, 1.8 FPS.

Without conditional rendering, the same compute check now runs, and a
full-screen pass with a small fragment shader reads its result and writes
the matching clear color, or discards. The CPU never waits. Integer formats,
which the shader's float output cannot write, still read back.

diff --git a/src/graphics/host_gpu/shaders/gpu_predicated_clear.frag b/src/graphics/host_gpu/shaders/gpu_predicated_clear.frag
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..35b9b85e
--- /dev/null
+++ b/src/graphics/host_gpu/shaders/gpu_predicated_clear.frag
@@ -0,0 +1,23 @@
+#version 450
+
+// Clears a color target to the key TileManager::CheckColorClear found for this slice, without
+// conditional rendering (which hangs the PS4's GPUs). Every pixel takes the same branch.
+layout(set = 0, binding = 0, std430) readonly buffer Predicates { uint data[]; } predicates;
+
+layout(push_constant, std430) uniform Clear {
+	vec4 colors[8]; // TileManager::ColorClearSlots
+	uint first;     // slice * ColorClearSlots
+	uint keys;
+} params;
+
+layout(location = 0) out vec4 color;
+
+void main() {
+	for (uint key = 0u; key < 8u; key++) {
+		if ((params.keys & (1u << key)) != 0u && predicates.data[params.first + key] != 0u) {
+			color = params.colors[key];
+			return;
+		}
+	}
+	discard;
+}
